    "q-118921": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118921",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253197/assets/7b676396ae24fe47c832e4442b67a9ba66128eff11a8c08f7570704c0a16eeb7.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find $|a+b|.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law of addition for $a$ and $b.$ We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane. The resultant goes from the start of $a$ to the head of $b.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253197/assets/87a40729c97eddcba2820dc083002aad9ee4d05d7e9e654bcf51d8410a2e4861.png)\n\nNow, in $△AHB$ we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=30\\,\\text{mm}$ and $BH=20\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{20}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1\\,300} \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{13}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
